# Files excluded from Vercel CLI uploads.
#
# HARD RULE: never list a path that the *build output* may legitimately
# reference — in practice `node_modules/` and `.next/`. Listing them here does
# not merely waste a line, it breaks production deploys:
#
#   Since Vercel CLI 58.4.4 (published 2026-07-30) `vercel deploy --prebuilt`
#   re-applies THIS file's rules to the `filePathMap` of every
#   `.vercel/output/functions/*.func/.vc-config.json`. Those maps point at the
#   traced sources under `node_modules/` and `.next/`, so a `node_modules` or
#   `.next` line here silently removes them from the upload (the drop is only
#   visible with `vercel deploy --debug`). The deploy then dies on Vercel's
#   side with:
#     Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, lstat '/vercel/path0/...'
#   Measured on this repo: those two lines alone dropped 2011 of 2012
#   filePathMap entries. That is what broke every production deploy from
#   2026-07-31 through 2026-08-12.
#   Upstream bug: https://github.com/vercel/vercel/issues/17386
#
# Both lines were redundant anyway: Vercel already ignores .git, .next,
# .vercel, node_modules, .env.local and .env.*.local by default.
# https://vercel.com/docs/builds/build-features#ignored-files-and-folders
#   "You do not need to add any of the above files and folders to your
#    .vercelignore file because it is done automatically by Vercel."

.next-backup
backup-before-cleanup
*.log
build-storybook.log
.storybook-static
storybook-static
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# Secrets. The .local variants duplicate Vercel's built-in defaults on purpose
# (belt and braces for credentials) and are verified not to shadow build output.
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.production.local
.env.preview
.env.staging
.env.vercel
.env.check
